  plt render --workflow <name>              the same, for a workflow named index, run or all
  plt render index|run <id>|all [--out <dir>] [--published <id|index> <url>]
                                             render the effort index / a run's status page from state into
                                             process/build/ (+ publish.json: which pages changed since the
                                             last render); --published records the page's url + artifact receipt;
                                             prints \`next: plt publish [<target>]\` when a page is behind its last publish
  plt publish [<index|run id>] [--out <dir>] [--project <dir>] [--json]
                                             list the rendered pages behind their last publish and print the exact
                                             Artifact call for each; it never publishes
  plt publish --record <index|run id> --url <url>
